<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ambrogio Spinola</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1569">1569</a>–1630</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ambrogio Spinola was a Genoese nobleman who became the leading general of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>'s armies in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/low-countries">Low Countries</a>. He took Ostend in 1604 after a three-year siege and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/breda">Breda</a> in 1625, a victory painted by Velázquez, and in 1620 he occupied the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palatinate-region">Lower Palatinate</a> early in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thirty-tyrants">the Thirty</a> Years' War. He died while campaigning in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> in 1630.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ambrogio-spinola.jpg" alt="Ambrogio Spinola" width="320" height="451" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Peter Paul Rubens · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Peter_Paul_Rubens_-_Portrait_of_Ambrogio_Spinola_-_WGA20376.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
